# Framework Jira issues (overlay)

## Gate

Requires the **`atlassian`** marketplace plugin. If `project.env` has blank
`DEFAULT_JIRA_PROJECT` **and** this turn has no named issue key and no
explicit Jira create/manage ask, **ignore this rule**.

Portable create / description / type craft lives in `atlassian-jira-create`,
`atlassian-jira-description`, `atlassian-jira-story`, `atlassian-jira-bug`,
`atlassian-jira-task`, `atlassian-jira-epic`, `atlassian-jira-subtask`. This
overlay only adds framework host wiring.

## Host defaults (`project.env`)

Prefer when set; never invent:

- `DEFAULT_JIRA_PROJECT`
- `DEFAULT_JIRA_BOARD_ID`
- `DEFAULT_JIRA_SITE_URL`
- `DEFAULT_JIRA_EPIC_KEY`
- `DEFAULT_JIRA_ASSIGNEE`

See `docs/examples/root/project.env.example`.

## Scope labels (required on create)

Every issue created for this monorepo must carry at least one:

| Label | When |
| --- | --- |
| `framework` | Base/substrate: runtimes, `applications/`, Docker/Compose, CI, scripts, Sphinx, shared policy, packaging |
| `addon` | Addon work under `framework/addons/` or ignored `addons/<name>/` |

Apply both when work spans both. Use invented wording only in examples
(`addons/<name>/`). Never name a real product addon in tracked policy.

## Create-and-implement → worktree

When the user adds an explicit implement verb after filing
(`atlassian-jira-create` create-and-implement), isolate under `code-worktrees`
/ `framework-git-workflow` (`git worktree add` under `~/.cursor/worktrees`;
`WORKTREE_DIR` only if that fails). Create-only asks still stop after filing.
